### Register a Citizen (any "role" field is ignored) — stores the access token
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha Patil",
  "email": "asha.{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}@example.test",
  "password": "citizen-pass-123",
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Log in as the bootstrap Admin (credentials from http-client.private.env.json)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Edit my profile
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha P.",
  "phone": "+919800000000"
}

### New access token from the refresh cookie (IntelliJ keeps cookies between requests)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Admin: create an Authority (needs a department id; departments are seeded in Phase 3)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ward Officer",
  "email": "officer.{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}@example.test",
  "password": "officer-pass-123",
  "role": "AUTHORITY",
  "departmentId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Admin: list users (page size capped at 50)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users?role=ADMIN&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log out (revokes the session and clears the cookie)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout
